  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting Vulnerable Communities to Build their Resilience to Human Smuggling and Human Trafficking through the Resilience Fund Project (24-0000591)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Implemented by the Global Initiative Against Transnational Organized Crime (GI-TOC) through the Resilience Fund, this five-year project strengthens the ability of civil society and local communities in Nigeria, Niger, Sudan, and Pakistan to prevent and respond to human smuggling and trafficking. By providing direct funding, capacity building, and regional collaboration, it empowers local actors to protect vulnerable migrants, reduce exploitation, and foster safer and more resilient communities</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="4">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aligns with the Netherlands Ministry of Foreign Affairs&#x2019; Migration and Displacement Grant Policy Framework 2023&#x2013;2028 and contributes to SDG 10.7, promoting orderly, safe, and responsible migration. It embeds gender equality, accountability, and locally led approaches, ensuring sustainability through long-term partnerships and knowledge exchange via the Resilience Fund Community Platform.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022; Civil society organizations, NGOs, and human rights defenders combating human trafficking and smuggling. &#x2022; Vulnerable migrants, potential victims, and host communities in high-risk areas of Nigeria, Niger, Sudan, and Pakistan. &#x2022; Local leaders and grassroots actors promoting human rights and community resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x2022; Protection and Assistance: Ensure that vulnerable migrants and potential victims of trafficking receive gender-sensitive protection and support. &#x2022; Community Response: Strengthen host communities&#x2019; capacity to prevent and respond to human trafficking and smuggling. &#x2022; Enabling Environment: Promote safe and enabling conditions for NGOs and human rights defenders advocating for migrants&#x2019; rights.</narrative>
  </description>
